  "scoreInterpretation": "Comparative observations against the original, fixed target and sealed round01, not a universal numeric approval threshold. Approval follows visible resolution of the prior mass/weight blocker, all-view style improvement and passing technical evidence.",
  "observations": [
    "The prior crystal/ore-cluster blocker is visibly resolved. E now has a broad blunt top plateau instead of an arrowhead apex. N lower stones have broad bearing silhouettes instead of a shield point, and W main/support masses no longer converge into an inverted point. These differences remain visible in the unscaled raw frames, logical sheet and phone placements.",
    "The stones now read as a weighty stepped rock bank: a larger crown leans subtly over smaller broad shoulders and ledges, and varied corner widths and side-plane angles keep the grouping coherent without the prior triangular gem pattern. The bright zigzag collars are replaced by solid, readable stone shoulders.",
    "Compared with the original native source, the object has visibly softer worn edge transitions and gentler cyan-to-cobalt turning planes. The lower N/W surfaces remain blue and readable rather than near-black blank slabs. Broad intentional faces remain graphic, but their softened corners and stepped surrounding masses provide sufficient volume at the intended scenery sizes.",
    "The blue palette family is preserved. Broad cyan upper planes, mid-blue bevel transitions and deeper cobalt lower planes describe volume consistently through all four facings. There are no white glare patches, exterior glow, copied speckles or preferred horizontal rim.",
    "All four views have deliberate stone grouping and convincing base width. No new side/rear dead spot, open end, dark patch, broken normal, clipping or geometry-overlap artifact was found. The five-piece native reconstruction is accepted on its visible outcome; neither old nor generated stone counts are constraints.",
    "At logical192x352 and smaller actual browser catalog placements, the crown/support hierarchy remains clear and the clean silhouette stays grounded. The repeated preview reads as repeated scenery without a false modular-join requirement.",
    "Phone, landscape and desktop actor/underwater previews preserve distinct submarine, eel, fish, bubbles and direction/warning silhouettes. The soft-blue bank reads as scenery rather than an excessive luminous beacon. The full underwater examples are explicitly browser-only inserted candidate placements, not production scene integration.",
    "The candidate remains simpler and less finely painted than the generated target. That difference is accepted: fine texture and exact cracks were not required, and the target one-sided warm rim/alpha fringe were correctly omitted. The required soft cartoon volume and broad grounded stone identity are present in the actual native exports."
  ],
